            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from statsmodels.tsa.stattools import adfuller\n",
        "\n",
        "def report_adf(series, label):\n",
        "    result = adfuller(series.dropna(), autolag=\"AIC\", result_object=True)\n",
        "    print(f\"{label}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  ADF statistic: {result.statistic:.4f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  p-value:       {result.pvalue:.6f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  used lags:     {result.lags}\")\n",
        "    for level, cv in result.critical_values.items():\n",
        "        print(f\"  critical value ({level}): {cv:.4f}\")\n",
        "    verdict = \"stationary (reject the unit-root null)\" if result.pvalue < 0.05 else \"NON-stationary (fail to reject the unit-root null)\"\n",
        "    print(f\"  => {verdict}\\n\")\n",
        "    return result.pvalue\n",
        "\n",
        "pvalue_raw = report_adf(series, \"Raw series\")\n",
        "pvalue_diff = report_adf(diffed, \"Once-differenced series\")"
      ],
      "id": "BPHqAo2oFGvQ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yTG1XLboFGvQ"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Interpreting the ADF test — and the differencing decision\n",
        "\n",
        "Run the cell above and read the p-values before treating the paragraph below\n",
        "as fact. On this series we expect **both** the raw and the once-differenced\n",
        "series to reject the unit-root null (raw p ≈ 0.002, differenced p ≈ 0.000),\n",
        "because `adfuller(..., autolag=\"AIC\")` defaults to `regression=\"c\"` — it\n",
        "tests against a constant mean, not against a deterministic *trend*. A\n",
        "stochastic unit root (a random walk) wanders off with no anchor and its\n",
        "variance grows without bound; this series has neither symptom, because the\n",
        "weekly seasonal cycle pulls it back toward a (slowly moving) baseline every\n",
        "few days. So the ADF is answering \"does this series wander off with no\n",
        "anchor?\" — and here the answer is no, on both the raw and differenced series.\n",
        "\n",
        "That does **not** mean the level is flat. The STL trend, the raw ACF's slow\n",
        "decay, and the yearly averages (627 → 679 → 702) all show a real upward\n",
        "drift. The lesson is that a hypothesis test is one input, not the whole\n",
        "decision, and that you have to check what `regression=` an ADF call defaults\n",
        "to before reading \"stationary\" as \"no trend at all.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "**Differencing decision — we do not difference.** Three reasons:\n",
        "1. The ADF test already rejects a unit root on the raw series, so a\n",
        "   difference is not required to make it stationary.\n",
        "2. A single lag-1 difference would not remove the weekly seasonality anyway —\n",
        "   the lag-7 spikes survive it, as the ACF/PACF section showed.\n",
        "3. The models we fit next each handle the trend and weekly cycle directly:\n",
        "   ETS with an additive trend and a period-7 seasonal term, and a LightGBM\n",
        "   with `lag_7` + calendar features. Differencing would add nothing but lost\n",
        "   information and a harder time interpreting the level.\n",
        "\n",
        "If we were instead fitting a plain (non-seasonal) ARIMA we would revisit\n",
        "`d=1` as a candidate — but that is not the family used here, so the series\n",
        "is kept in its original level."
