      "source": [
        "## Section 3 — ML/GBM Forecasting & Feature Engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "A tree model has no notion of \"yesterday\" or \"last week\" built in — unlike\n",
        "ETS or ARIMA, it sees each row as independent numbers with no memory of row\n",
        "order. Every bit of time structure has to be handed to it explicitly as a\n",
        "feature. This section engineers lag/rolling/calendar features, then\n",
        "implements **recursive multi-step forecasting**, where each step's\n",
        "prediction feeds the next step's lags.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Temporal feature engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "`make_features` turns a plain `units_sold` series into a table a tree model\n",
        "can learn from: lags at four horizons, three rolling statistics, and calendar\n",
        "signals. Every lag/rolling feature is built from `y.shift(1)` (or later) so\n",
        "the feature for date `t` only uses days *before* `t`, never `t`'s own value."
      ],
      "id": "OEiPDESNFGvQ"
    },
