      "source": [
        "### Leakage risk — why features are rebuilt inside each fold\n",
        "\n",
        "The single easiest way to make a forecast look better than it is, on this\n",
        "kind of model, is to build the features once on the full series and then\n",
        "reuse that same table inside every fold. The individual lag/rolling values\n",
        "would still look \"correct\" (they only look backward from each row), but\n",
        "anything *stateful* fit the same way would not: a `StandardScaler`, a target\n",
        "encoder, or a model fit on the whole series before the fold loop would hand a\n",
        "fold's training rows a mean/statistic computed using data that, from that\n",
        "fold's point of view, has not happened yet. That is leakage.\n",
        "\n",
        "Two rules keep this sound here:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **A feature at date `t` may use only strictly-earlier values.** `lag_1`,\n",
        "   the rolling means/std, and the calendar fields all obey this — the\n",
        "   `lag_*`/`roll_*` columns are built from `y.shift(1)` or later, so `y[t]`\n",
        "   itself is never an input to the row for date `t`.\n",
        "2. **Features must be recomputed inside each fold on that fold's history only\n",
        "   — never computed once on the full series.** In this notebook the LightGBM\n",
        "   callable rebuilds `make_features(history)` fresh inside the fold callable\n",
        "   from `y_train` alone. Fold 0's model has therefore literally never seen a\n",
        "   feature value derived from 2025 data.\n",
        "\n",
        "The same property must survive the **recursive** forecast: predicting step 2\n",
        "requires `lag_1`, which is step 1's *prediction*, not a true future value.\n",
        "The recursive loop below feeds each prediction back into the working history\n",
        "before computing the next step's features — it never reaches for the real\n",
        "value sitting in the holdout set."
      ],
      "id": "knNndbGzFGvQ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gnY5_G6XFGvQ"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Recursive LightGBM forecaster\n",
        "\n",
        "`lightgbm_recursive_fit_predict(y_train, horizon)` is a single callable with\n",
        "the exact signature `run_backtest` expects. It fits a fresh model on the\n",
        "given `y_train` only, then forecasts one day at a time, feeding each\n",
        "prediction back in as the next step's lag. Because every fold's training\n",
        "slice starts at the series' first date (`expanding_window_splits` guarantees\n",
        "this), we can reconstruct real calendar dates inside the callable from\n",
        "`SERIES_START` plus a position count — no need to thread dates through\n",
        "`run_backtest` itself."
      ],
      "id": "gnY5_G6XFGvQ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Rzn0f9cCFGvR"
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import lightgbm as lgb\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def lightgbm_recursive_fit_predict(y_train, horizon):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Fit fresh on this fold's y_train only, then forecast recursively.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Features are recomputed inside this callable on THIS fold's\n",
        "    reconstructed history — never on the full series computed once outside\n",
        "    the fold loop — so a model trained on one fold has never seen a feature\n",
        "    value derived from a later fold's data. Recursive: each prediction is\n",
        "    appended to the working history and becomes the next step's lag.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    idx = pd.date_range(start=SERIES_START, periods=len(y_train), freq=\"D\")\n",
        "    history = pd.Series(y_train, index=idx)\n",
        "\n",
        "    train_feat = make_features(history).dropna()\n",
        "    model = lgb.LGBMRegressor(\n",
        "        n_estimators=200,\n",
        "        num_leaves=15,\n",
        "        learning_rate=0.05,\n",
        "        min_child_samples=10,\n",
        "        random_state=RNG_SEED,\n",
        "        verbosity=-1,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    model.fit(train_feat[FEATURE_COLS], train_feat[\"y\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "    working = history.copy()\n",
        "    preds = []\n",
        "    for _ in range(horizon):\n",
        "        next_date = working.index[-1] + pd.Timedelta(days=1)\n",
        "        extended = pd.concat([working, pd.Series([np.nan], index=[next_date])])\n",
        "        next_feat = make_features(extended).loc[[next_date], FEATURE_COLS]\n",
        "        pred = float(model.predict(next_feat)[0])\n",
        "        preds.append(pred)\n",
        "        # the prediction becomes part of the working history that feeds the\n",
        "        # NEXT step's lag/rolling features — this is what makes the forecast\n",
        "        # recursive instead of leaking true future values.\n",
        "        working.loc[next_date] = pred\n",
        "    return np.array(preds)"
      ],
      "id": "Rzn0f9cCFGvR"
    },
