    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "WDD-9m1zFGvR"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Three models, one interface\n",
        "\n",
        "Each model is wrapped as a `fit_predict_fn(y_train, horizon)`; `run_backtest`\n",
        "calls it fresh for every fold, so refitting per fold is automatic. The harness\n",
        "guarantees no fold's training data overlaps its own test window — the callable\n",
        "is handed only `y_train`, and never sees a single value from its own or any\n",
        "later fold's test window."
      ],
      "id": "WDD-9m1zFGvR"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "lnMRv1LmFGvR",
        "outputId": "ec00d397-30e8-4489-af1d-cf9742c35642"
      },
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "ran 5 folds: seasonal-naive\n",
            "ran 5 folds: Holt-Winters\n",
            "ran 5 folds: LightGBM (recursive)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def naive_fit_predict(y_train, horizon):\n",
        "    \"\"\"The floor every model here is expected to beat: repeat the last\n",
        "    observed weekly cycle. No fitting at all — same call signature as the\n",
        "    other two so it can go through the exact same run_backtest loop.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return seasonal_naive_forecast(y_train, horizon, period=SEASONAL_PERIOD)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def holt_winters_fit_predict(y_train, horizon):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Fit a fresh Holt-Winters model on exactly this fold's y_train and\n",
        "    forecast `horizon` steps ahead. Refitting inside the callable (rather\n",
        "    than fitting once outside the fold loop) is what makes this a fair\n",
        "    walk-forward comparison.\"\"\"\n",
        "    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n",
        "        warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\")\n",
        "        model = ExponentialSmoothing(\n",
        "            y_train, trend=\"add\", seasonal=\"add\", seasonal_periods=SEASONAL_PERIOD\n",
        "        ).fit()\n",
        "    return model.forecast(horizon)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "naive_results = run_backtest(series.values, splits, naive_fit_predict)\n",
        "hw_results = run_backtest(series.values, splits, holt_winters_fit_predict)\n",
        "lgb_results = run_backtest(series.values, splits, lightgbm_recursive_fit_predict)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"ran {len(naive_results)} folds: seasonal-naive\")\n",
        "print(f\"ran {len(hw_results)} folds: Holt-Winters\")\n",
        "print(f\"ran {len(lgb_results)} folds: LightGBM (recursive)\")"
      ],
      "id": "lnMRv1LmFGvR"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tVxTN7thFGvR"
      },
      "source": [
        "**A concrete leakage check.** Inside `lightgbm_recursive_fit_predict`,\n",
        "`history = pd.Series(y_train, index=idx)` is a Series built fresh from that\n",
        "fold's `y_train` only, and `train_feat = make_features(history).dropna()` runs\n",
        "once per fold call on that history alone. Fold 0's `train_feat` is built from\n",
        "a `history` that only ever contains 2023's early days, because `y_train`\n",
        "itself only contains those days; and `lgb.LGBMRegressor(...)` is instantiated\n",
        "and `.fit()` inside the same callable, so fold 0's trained model has never\n",
        "seen a single row derived from 2025. Contrast that with the leaking version —\n",
        "computing `make_features(series)` once on the full series before `splits` is\n",
        "built and slicing it per fold — which is exactly the bug we avoid here."
      ],
      "id": "tVxTN7thFGvR"
    },
